# Shared cust web cleanup

Current Passenger Link stays as it is until it is replaced. The new flow is a flag, not a rewrite of the old app.

- Missing or `N` for `VITE_NEW_PASSENGER_LINK`: `POST /passenger_link/webApp/initWebApp`, `POST /passenger_link/webApp/getMyTrips`, phone-login key `initWebApp`, price check `bookNewJob`. Legends booking stays on in code. Other companies still turn booking off when `BOOKING_ENABLED=N`.
- `VITE_NEW_PASSENGER_LINK=Y` only, and only in the website env: init is `POST /custWeb/initCustWebApp`, booking stays on, price check is `refreshRates`. Do not set this on the passengerlink env.
- New shared logic goes in `CustWebAppService` and `CustWebBookingController`. `WebAppService` stays the current Passenger Link service.
- Shared HTTP mappings live on `CustWebBookingController`.
- Each `BookingController` keeps only calls that are still unique to that app.
- Do not copy a response map or look up the same data in a second service.
- The full init body includes fields either side needs.

```java
// passenger link
return webAppService.initWebApp();
// legends website
return custWebAppService.initCustWebApp();
```
